{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-58",
  "title": "Comcast Franchise Agreement",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Comcast Franchise Agreement"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[Legislative File](https://lims.minneapolismn.gov/File/2020-00392)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Effective: Apr 4, 2020"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Comcast's requests for cable television franchise agreement renewals involve a process that's both complex and closely regulated by federal law. These agreements authorize Comcast to install and operate cable systems in public rights-of-way, in exchange for providing cable services to residents and meeting other obligations like offering public access channels and supporting local programming."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To \"provide cable services\" in the context of a cable television franchise agreement typically involves several key components:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Infrastructure and Access**: The cable provider, such as Comcast, installs and maintains the physical infrastructure needed to deliver cable television services. This includes cables, distribution boxes, and other necessary equipment installed in public rights-of-way or on utility poles to bring the cable signal to subscribers' homes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Television Programming**: Providing cable services also means offering a variety of television channels and programming to subscribers. This can range from local and national news, sports, entertainment, educational content, and premium channels, depending on the service package chosen by the subscriber."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Customer Service**: Part of the obligation of providing cable services includes offering customer support for subscribers. This involves addressing issues related to billing, service disruptions, equipment problems, and general inquiries to ensure customer satisfaction."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To \"support local programming\" involves a few distinct actions:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Public Access Channels**: Cable providers often agree to include public, educational, and government access (PEG) channels as part of their service offering. These channels are reserved for local content, such as city council meetings, local educational programming, and community events, providing a platform for local voices and public interest content."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Funding and Resources**: Supporting local programming can also involve providing funding, equipment, and studio space to local organizations, schools, or government entities to produce content for PEG channels. This support enables high-quality production values for local content and encourages community participation in content creation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Promotion of Local Content**: Part of the support for local programming may include the promotion of these local access channels within the cable service's channel lineup and through other marketing efforts. This helps ensure that subscribers are aware of the local programming available to them."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In summary, providing cable services encompasses the physical delivery of television content to subscribers, along with customer service support, while supporting local programming focuses on fostering local content creation, offering public access channels, and ensuring the community has a platform for local voices and content."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the City of Bellingham, for example, the franchise agreement with Comcast was set to expire in November 2021, with previous renewals involving assessments of community needs, technological, financial, and communication considerations, and negotiations on cable-related benefits to meet those needs over the new term【8†source】. Similarly, in Calvert County, Maryland, the renewal process emphasized extending cable service to unserved areas, with a significant commitment of county funding to complete Comcast cable infrastructure buildout, ensuring wider access to cable services【9†source】."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nashua, NH, also underwent a franchise renewal process with Comcast for the term 2022-2032, which, like other jurisdictions, included negotiations over the franchise fee - a percentage of Comcast’s gross cable television revenue - and considerations about public, education, and government (PEG) access channels. These franchise fees and the inclusion of PEG channels are common aspects of such agreements, reflecting the community benefits negotiated in exchange for the use of public rights-of-way【10†source】."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "These examples highlight the importance of local government involvement in negotiating the terms of franchise agreements to ensure they meet the evolving needs of their communities while complying with federal regulations. The renewal process typically involves public input, assessment of community cable needs, and negotiations over the terms and benefits included in the franchise agreement."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Sources:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
